3,Yekora language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/yekora_language,"Yekora (ISO 639-3: ykr) is a Papuan language of the Trans-New Guinea phylum, specifically within the Binanderean branch, spoken by approximately 2,100 people (as of 2023) in two villages near the Morobe government station in Morobe Province, Papua New Guinea. [1] [2] It is classified under the Greater Binanderean family and is considered vigorous, with no immediate endangerment concerns. [1 ...",Yekora,Trans-New Guinea
